{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"advisory":[{"agreement":1,"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Guard the force-close completion_signature assignment on `current_status != \"idea\"` so `idea -> closed --force` carries no marker, matching the documented reject/drop contract.","criteria":["correctness","edge-cases","regression"],"decision":"advisory","evidence":["src/rebar/_commands/transition_close.py:505: `if target_status == \"closed\" and force_close:`","src/rebar/_commands/transition_close.py:508: `completion_signature = {\"signed\": False, \"cause\": \"force_bypassed\", \"error\": \"\"}`","src/rebar/_commands/transition_close.py:414: `if target_status == \"closed\" and current_status != \"idea\":` (the sign path DOES exclude idea)","types.py comment: 'read its absence as \"not a completion close\" (a plain transition, or `idea -> closed`, which is a REJECT/DROP rather than a completion)'","src/rebar/_commands/transition.py:563: CLI derives `force_close=(force_reason or \"(no reason given)\") if force else \"\"`, so any `--force` close (including idea->closed) makes force_close truthy","src/rebar/_commands/txn.py:251: `idea -> closed` is a legal transition and --force is not blocked on it, so the path is reachable and untested (idea->closed test uses no --force)"],"finding":"A `--force` close FROM the `idea` status sets completion_signature={cause: force_bypassed}, contradicting the documented contract that `idea -> closed` carries NO marker (a REJECT/DROP is not a completion). The force-close block guards only on `target_status == \"closed\" and force_close`, not on `current_status != \"idea\"`, unlike the completion-precheck block which excludes idea.","id":"0","impact":0.3,"location":"